# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must NOT be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `.gitignore` governs git; it does NOT govern what the
# Vercel CLI uploads. Without this file the first deployment shipped `.env` —
# real source and application database passwords, and the Gemini key — into the
# deployment bundle, where they are outside secret management and cannot be
# rotated from the dashboard. Nothing in `.gitignore` prevented it, because
# nothing in `.gitignore` was being consulted.
#
# Environment variables belong in Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets. Never upload. -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env

*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
secrets.json

# --- CST rule documents -----------------------------------------------------
# Both casings: the folder is `knowledge-source` on a case-insensitive Windows
# disk and matching is case-sensitive elsewhere, so one pattern is not enough.
#
# THE RULE WORKBOOKS SHIP; THE CUSTOMER LIST NEVER DOES.
#
# Excluding the whole folder was the safe first move, and it turned out to be
# the wrong finished answer. The deployed application still needs these files
# at runtime — not to generate a draft (OpenAI retrieves the rules from the
# vector store) but to turn a stored citation like WROITE-MAJ-15 back into the
# rule a reviewer can read. Without them, production resolved citations against
# whatever happened to be in the bundle and reported the rest as "no longer
# exist in the current documents", which was untrue: the documents were fine,
# they simply were not deployed.
#
# The pattern below excludes the CONTENTS rather than the directory, because a
# file cannot be re-included once its parent directory is excluded. The final
# rule re-excludes "B2B  customers .xlsx", which carries customer contact data
# and must never leave this machine. Later patterns win, so that rule is last.
/Knowledge-source/*
!/Knowledge-source/*.xlsx
/Knowledge-source/B2B*

/knowledge-source/*
!/knowledge-source/*.xlsx
/knowledge-source/B2B*

# --- Not needed at runtime --------------------------------------------------
# Keeps the serverless bundle down; the build already warns that dynamic
# filesystem access causes the whole project to be traced into it.
/tests/
/scripts/
/migrations/
/.claude/

# --- Local artefacts --------------------------------------------------------
*.tsbuildinfo
/coverage/
/.next/
/node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Rendered knowledge documents (review artefact of knowledge:sync).
/.knowledge-build/

# Scheduler output.
/logs/
